---
source: crates/biome_css_analyze/tests/spec_tests.rs
expression: invalid.scss
---
# Input
```css
/* should generate diagnostics */
@use "sass:math";

$gap: 8px;
$path: "a.png";

:root {
	--gap: $gap;
	--pi: math.$pi;
	--calc: calc($gap * 2);
	--fallback: var(--x, $gap);
	--url: url($path);
	--list: $gap $gap;
	--braced: {a: $gap};
	--commented:
		/* before */ $gap /* after */;
	--own-line:
		math.$pi;
	--url-module: url(t.$path);
	--sass-call: darken($gap, 10%);
	--module-call: math.max($gap, 1px);
}

@supports (--raw: $gap) {
	a {
		color: red;
	}
}

@container style(--c: $gap) {
	a {
		color: red;
	}
}

```

# Diagnostics
```
invalid.scss:8:9 lint/nursery/noUninterpolatedScssVariable  FIXABLE  ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  × The Sass variable $gap isn't interpolated, so Sass outputs it unchanged.
  
     7 │ :root {
   > 8 │ 	--gap: $gap;
       │ 	       ^^^^
     9 │ 	--pi: math.$pi;
    10 │ 	--calc: calc($gap * 2);
  
  i Sass only evaluates #{...} inside custom property values, so the browser receives the text $gap instead of the variable's value.
  
  i This rule belongs to the nursery group, which means it is not yet stable and may change in the future. Visit https://biomejs.dev/linter/#nursery for more information.
  
  i Unsafe fix: Wrap the variable in interpolation.
  
    8 │ → --gap:·#{$gap};
      │          ++    + 

```

